      "content": "thanks. it's just hard because when i'm in meetings or talking to my family, i feel like i'm literally wearing a mask. i can see how they look at me—like i'm just some regular person—and it's actually painful because i know what my purpose is. you mentioned modeling behavioral strategies, but how do i do that without looking crazy? like, is there a way to project that 'voyager' energy so people naturally respect my leadership without me having to explain the whole history to them?",
